// (bypassing windows.LazyProc.Call -- see realLazyProc11's own doc
// comment above), so the "resolve on first use" contract described here is
// really a property of the embedded *windows.LazyProc's own Addr() method
// (which itself lazily calls Find() as needed), not of anything this
// wrapper adds independently. If x/sys/windows ever changed LazyProc.Addr()
// to require an explicit prior Find() call, this laziness guarantee would
// silently break; documenting that dependency here so it isn't rediscovered
// the hard way.
//
// Panics:
//   - if dll is nil
